({{ v('recovery.own.rho_09_feedback_on.rank_agreement_lower') }} to
{{ v('recovery.own.rho_09_feedback_on.rank_agreement_upper') }}) with feedback on and
{{ v('recovery.own.rho_09_feedback_off.rank_agreement') }}
({{ v('recovery.own.rho_09_feedback_off.rank_agreement_lower') }} to
{{ v('recovery.own.rho_09_feedback_off.rank_agreement_upper') }}) with it off.
{% endif %}
Every channel and condition, with intervals over seeds:

{{ table('recovery.own.summary') }}

{{ label('recovery.own.summary') }}

**Calibration.** The lift test on {{ v('calibrate.channel')|lower }} moved that channel's return from
{{ v('calibrate.own.roas_before') }} to {{ v('calibrate.own.roas_after') }} against a true
{{ v('calibrate.own.roas_true') }}; the interval {{ 'covered' if raw('calibrate.own.covers_before') == 'yes' else 'missed' }}
the truth before and {{ 'covers' if raw('calibrate.own.covers_after') == 'yes' else 'misses' }} it after,
because the experiment's estimate sits {{ 'above' if raw('geo.did.estimate') > raw('geo.truth') else 'below' }}
the truth and the calibrated fit follows it. Across {{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.seeds') }} seeds, each
with its own test, the error on the tested channel went from
{{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.tested_error_before') }} to {{ v('calibrate.own.recovery.tested_error_after') }}.

{{ table('calibrate.own.before_after') }}

{{ label('calibrate.own.before_after') }}

{{ table('calibrate.own.recovery') }}

{{ label('calibrate.own.recovery') }}
{% endset %}
{% set contract %}
{% call m.line('trained', 'met') %}
Fit in the pipeline (`make recovery`) on the {{ v('sim.weeks') }} weeks of the demonstration panel, with the transform search scored on {{ v('policy.rolling_origins') }} rolling origins held out in time, and its plan judged on the true curves against last year's mix and an equal split (the `budget.comparison` table in the memo).
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('timed', 'met') %}
The panel runs from {{ v('sim.first_week') }} to {{ v('sim.last_week') }} and the manifest is as of {{ manifest.as_of }}; the fit sees no week after the panel's last, and the lift test it is calibrated on ran inside the panel, weeks {{ v('geo.start_week') }} to {{ v('geo.end_week') }}.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('calibrated', 'partly') %}
Its {{ v('policy.interval_level') }} bootstrap intervals are checked against the truth and fall short: they cover it in {{ v('mmm.own.covered_count') }} of {{ v('policy.channel_count') }} channels here and {{ v('recovery.own.coverage_overall') }} of the time across the recovery study.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('useful', 'met') %}
It sets the weekly plan: at the {{ v('policy.contribution_margin') }} contribution margin its calibrated curves move last year's {{ v('budget.total_weekly') }} a week between channels for a true gain of {{ v('budget.headline.gain_over_last_year_weekly') }} a week on the demonstration brand.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('fair', 'not applicable') %}
Not applicable to people, because the model sees weekly national spend and sales and no customer; the parties a plan affects are the channels and the teams behind them, and the change limit of {{ v('policy.budget_max_change_share') }} bounds how far one plan moves any of them.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('gated', 'partly') %}
Tests check that every step of the search and the bootstrap ran and that a fit is reproducible from its seed, and the recovery stage counts the fits that ran ({{ v('recovery.own.fits_that_ran') }} of {{ v('recovery.own.fits') }}); no diagnostic bound fails an own fit.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('served', 'met') %}
The API loads the calibrated export ({{ v('budget.model_version') }}) when `results/calibrate/own_calibrated_model.json` exists and the uncalibrated one otherwise, answers `/v1/optimize` and `/v1/plans` with it and names it in `/v1/health` and `/v1/models`; when a separate client last checked the live instance ({{ v('deploy.checked_at') }}) it named {{ v('deploy.model_version') }}.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('integrated', 'met') %}
The budget stage builds the plan from its curves, the attribution stage reads its channel shares, and the site's Mix and Budget pages draw its returns, curves and plan from the marts.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('monitored', 'not built') %}
There is no scheduled refit or drift check, and the weekly refresh is a stretch goal; what exists is the recovery study, rerun with the pipeline, and its log in `logs/recovery_own.log`.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('documented', 'met') %}
This card, `docs/models.md` and `docs/evaluation.md`, all rendered from the manifest by the claim gate.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('bounded', 'met') %}
The statement closes this card: the brand is fictional and the market simulated, so every return here describes the simulator.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('validated', 'met') %}
Graded against the simulator's known truth, never against itself: the truth sits beside every estimate on the demonstration brand, and the recovery study grades {{ v('recovery.own.fits') }} fits across {{ v('recovery.own.conditions') }} conditions.
{% endcall %}
{% call m.line('explainable at the decision', 'met') %}
A reader of the plan sees each channel's return with its interval and the truth, the response curves on the Mix page, and in the allocation table the marginal return, the marginal profit and the bound each channel sits at.
{% endcall %}
{% endset %}
{% set limitations %}
The intervals are too narrow. The bootstrap holds carryover and saturation at their searched
values, so the uncertainty of the search itself is left out, and coverage in the recovery study is
{{ v('recovery.own.coverage_overall') }} against a stated {{ v('policy.interval_level') }}. Quote bayes's
intervals, or treat these as a floor, before reading a channel's interval as the range of its
return.

The error in return is {{ 'over the stated floor in every condition of the recovery study' if floor_all else 'over the stated floor in some conditions of the recovery study' }},
and worst in {{ v('recovery.own.worst_condition') }}{% if raw('recovery.own.worst_condition').startswith('rho 0.9') %},
where the channels' spend moves most closely together: a brand that plans every channel on the
same calendar gives this model the least to learn from{% endif %}.

The Nelder-Mead step stops at its evaluation cap rather than at a convergence test, so a longer
search could move the transforms.

The simulator was written with the model family this backend fits, so the recovery study measures
estimation error, not the error of assuming the wrong family.

Calibration pulls the tested channel toward one experiment, and that experiment sits
{{ 'above' if raw('geo.did.estimate') > raw('geo.truth') else 'below' }} the truth; with one test the
model cannot tell the experiment's error from its own.
{% endset %}
